; case: counter-width-and-rate
; verdict: accept
; ambiguous: yes
; tests: externality=pass implementation-independence=pass non-prescription=pass
; rationale: AMBIGUOUS, resolved ACCEPT. The width and rate of an offered counter look like
;   implementation trivia, but they are architectural facts a substituting implementation must
;   also have: they decide the unambiguous horizon, the programmable range and the conversion
;   arithmetic. ROADMAP.md §4.3 admits "an offered modular-counter width/rate where
;   architecturally relevant" in exactly these words. The test that settles it is
;   implementation-independence: a different timer with the same width and rate is
;   interchangeable here, so the field describes the interface, not the part.
; other-side: engine: whether to extend the epoch, how often to read, and the arithmetic that
;   follows from these facts
;
(defblock timer.counter
  (offers
    (counter-width 32 bit)
    (counter-modulus 4294967296)
    (tick-rate 10 MHz)))
